      "writtenOn": "2024-01-10T16:53:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why not just `assert!(matches!(e, ....), \"Unexpected error {e:?}\");` ?\n\nAlso, given how it\u0027s used, why not make it:\n```rust\nfn assert_not_found(result: Result\u003cSecret, Error\u003e) {\n    assert!(matches!(result, Err(Error::SecretkeeperError(SecretkeeperError::EntryNotFound)), \"Unexpected error {result:?}\")\n}\n```\n\nand then all the callers will just be:\n\n```rust\n    assert_not_found(sk_client.get(\u0026ID_NOT_STORED));\n```",
      "range": {
